 past the deadline, model warm or cold. The test holds one row per failure value plus a warm row and a cold-inside-deadline row, six rows in total.\n\n  Line 95: Setup records the before numbers, the hook timing and the cold-load behaviour after an aborted call. Implementation adds the script, the deadline, the status fields, the warning, the route, the setup leg and the guide text in the waves `tasks.md` lists. Verification reruns the script, both captures, the floor, the rollup, the hook timing and both test suites. The ordered work and each task's check are in `tasks.md`.\n\n  Line 105: | Unit | The prompt embedding with an injected adapter: warm, cold inside the deadline, absent, model missing, past the deadline and the warning | Vitest, `tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` with `VITEST` stubbed off inside the test |\n\n  Line 147: | Implementation | The before numbers and the cold-load reading | Verification |\n","title":"grep","metadata":{"metadata":{"matches":9,"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found 9 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/plan.md:\n  Line 29: The change adds one measurement script, two fields in the semantic lane health, one warning, one deadline, one doctor route and one `/doctor:setup` leg. It also rewrites the install guides from the script's output. The state is read where it already lives: the active pointer, the two vector tables and one `/api/tags` call. The proof is the script's JSON, the four degrade tests, the route contract test and unchanged captures.\n\n  Line 45: - [ ] `npx vitest run tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 0 failed, and `bash DOC/scripts/tests/run-all.sh` reports 0 failed.\n\n  Line 55: Probe, plan, approve. The read paths report state, the route acts only after a yes and the scorer degrades on its own clock.\n\n  Line 76: | `withSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding` | Embeds the prompt for the cosine lane, waits up to the adapter's 5,000 ms | Update: deadline and distinct reasons | `tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` |\n\n  Line 78: | `outputWarnings` | Warns on a stale graph or a degraded lane | Update: one more warning | The degrade test's warning case |\n\n  Line 87: Matrix axes for the degrade test: server reachable or absent, model pulled or missing, answer inside or past the deadline, model warm or cold. The test holds one row per failure value plus a warm row and a cold-inside-deadline row, six rows in total.\n\n  Line 95: Setup records the before numbers, the hook timing and the cold-load behaviour after an aborted call. Implementation adds the script, the deadline, the status fields, the warning, the route, the setup leg and the guide text in the waves `tasks.md` lists. Verification reruns the script, both captures, the floor, the rollup, the hook timing and both test suites. The ordered work and each task's check are in `tasks.md`.\n\n  Line 105: | Unit | The prompt embedding with an injected adapter: warm, cold inside the deadline, absent, model missing, past the deadline and the warning | Vitest, `tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` with `VITEST` stubbed off inside the test |\n\n  Line 147: | Implementation | The before numbers and the cold-load reading | Verification |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/plan.md\",\"pattern\":\"degrade|matrix|VITEST|300 ms|cold|never arrives\"}"},"time":{"start":1794535028076,"end":1794535028766}}}}
