{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794535037141,"sessionID":"ses_e2d61a837fferT6vx7XBcnnvGb","part":{"partID":"prt_1d29f9858002DtUzImzx2htT4p","sessionID":"ses_e2d61a837fferT6vx7XBcnnvGb","messageID":"msg_1d29f8ee8001t8PEcoRFOWMvAh","type":"tool","id":"call_f2ee693116bb4e108689be1e","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/plan.md","offset":60,"limit":60},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/plan.md, lines 60-119\n60: - **Prompt embedding deadline** (`withSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding` in `ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts`): without it a hung server holds the call for 5,000 ms and the Claude hook drops the brief at 2,500 ms.\n61: - **Warning** (`outputWarnings` in `ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`): without it a caller cannot tell a phrase-only answer from a full one. The operator chose this surface over a brief line.\n62: - **Doctor route** (`DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml`): without it no path sets the embedder up, and `rebuild` writes vectors only by side effect.\n63: - **Setup leg** (`DOC/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`): without it `/doctor:setup`, the command `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` sends every new user to, says nothing about the embedder.\n64: \n65: ### Data Flow\n66: At recommend time the handler embeds the prompt once inside the deadline. A failure or a timeout sets `disabledReason`, the scorer runs on phrases and `outputWarnings` reads the reason into `semantic_lane_off:<reason>`. At status time `readSemanticLaneHealth` reads the pointer and both vector tables and asks `/api/tags` once. `/doctor:setup` and the route read that status. After a yes the route runs the approved steps, then `skill_graph_scan --trusted`, which embeds skills and commands as phase 004 built it.\n67: <!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n68: \n69: ---\n70: \n71: <!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n72: ## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n73: \n74: | Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n75: |---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n76: | `withSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding` | Embeds the prompt for the cosine lane, waits up to the adapter's 5,000 ms | Update: deadline and distinct reasons | `tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` |\n77: | `readSemanticLaneHealth` and its schema | Reports pointer, skill coverage and the last reason | Update: `backend` and `commandVectorCoverage` | `tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` |\n78: | `outputWarnings` | Warns on a stale graph or a degraded lane | Update: one more warning | The degrade test's warning case |\n79: | `readEmbeddingsHealth` (`ADV/lib/embedders/embeddings-health.ts`) | Probes the hf-local socket | Unchanged, the guide says what it probes | REQ-011 |\n80: | `OllamaAdapter` and `OLLAMA_QUERY_TIMEOUT_MS` (`system-spec-kit/shared`) | Shared deadline for every query embedding | Unchanged. The deadline lives in the advisor's wrapper so other consumers keep 5,000 ms | `git diff --stat` shows no file under `system-spec-kit/shared` |\n81: | `/doctor:setup` | Five read-only legs | Update: sixth leg | `DOC/scripts/tests/run-all.sh` |\n82: | `/doctor:install` | Five printed steps | Update: the embedder route becomes step 5 and `/doctor:setup` step 6 | `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` |\n83: | `/doctor:skill-advisor` | Six routes | Update: seventh route | `skill-advisor-route-contract.test.cjs`, `route-validate.sh`, `doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` |\n84: | Command bridge inventory | 45 TypeScript rows with `embeddingText` | Update: the route's bridge becomes active like its six siblings | Both captures and the policy rollup |\n85: | Hook brief (`ADV/lib/render.ts`) | Renders the brief | Unchanged, by the operator's answer of 2026-11-12 | Golden briefs unchanged in `npm test` |\n86: \n87: Matrix axes for the degrade test: server reachable or absent, model pulled or missing, answer inside or past the deadline, model warm or cold. The test holds one row per failure value plus a warm row and a cold-inside-deadline row, six rows in total.\n88: <!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n89: \n90: ---\n91: \n92: <!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n93: ## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n94: \n95: Setup records the before numbers, the hook timing and the cold-load behaviour after an aborted call. Implementation adds the script, the deadline, the status fields, the warning, the route, the setup leg and the guide text in the waves `tasks.md` lists. Verification reruns the script, both captures, the floor, the rollup, the hook timing and both test suites. The ordered work and each task's check are in `tasks.md`.\n96: <!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n97: \n98: ---\n99: \n100: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n101: ## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n102: \n103: | Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n104: |-----------|-------|-------|\n105: | Unit | The prompt embedding with an injected adapter: warm, cold inside the deadline, absent, model missing, past the deadline and the warning | Vitest, `tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` with `VITEST` stubbed off inside the test |\n106: | Unit | Status `backend` states and `commandVectorCoverage` against fixture databases | Vitest, `tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` |\n107: | Integration | The route's plan-first contract, the setup leg and the install step | `bash DOC/scripts/tests/run-all.sh`, `bash DOC/scripts/route-validate.sh`, `node DOC/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` |\n108: | Integration | Captures, floor and rollup unchanged with the new bridge active | `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` with and without `--real-embedding`, `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs` |\n109: | Manual | The script on the build machine, once warm and once after the 5 minute unload | `node ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs` |\n110: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n111: \n112: ---\n113: \n114: <!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n115: ## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n116: \n117: | Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n118: |------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n119: | Ollama 0.40.15 with `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` | External | Green: running on 2026-11-12 | No measured numbers. The tests still run with an injected adapter |\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 120]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/plan.md, lines 60-119\n60: - **Prompt embedding deadline** (`withSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding` in `ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts`): without it a hung server holds the call for 5,000 ms and the Claude hook drops the brief at 2,500 ms.\n61: - **Warning** (`outputWarnings` in `ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`): without it a caller cannot tell a phrase-only answer from a full one. The operator chose this surface over a brief line.\n62: - **Doctor route** (`DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml`): without it no path sets the embedder up, and `rebuild` writes vectors only by side effect.\n63: - **Setup leg** (`DOC/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`): without it `/doctor:setup`, the command `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` sends every new user to, says nothing about the embedder.\n64: \n65: ### Data Flow\n66: At recommend time the handler embeds the prompt once inside the deadline. A failure or a timeout sets `disabledReason`, the scorer runs on phrases and `outputWarnings` reads the reason into `semantic_lane_off:<reason>`. At status time `readSemanticLaneHealth` reads the pointer and both vector tables and asks `/api/tags` once. `/doctor:setup` and the route read that status. After a yes the route runs the approved steps, then `skill_graph_scan --trusted`, which embeds skills and commands as phase 004 built it.\n67: <!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n68: \n69: ---\n70: \n71: <!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n72: ## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n73: \n74: | Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n75: |---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n76: | `withSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding` | Embeds the prompt for the cosine lane, waits up to the adapter's 5,000 ms | Update: deadline and distinct reasons | `tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` |\n77: | `readSemanticLaneHealth` and its schema | Reports pointer, skill coverage and the last reason | Update: `backend` and `commandVectorCoverage` | `tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` |\n78: | `outputWarnings` | Warns on a stale graph or a degraded lane | Update: one more warning | The degrade test's warning case |\n79: | `readEmbeddingsHealth` (`ADV/lib/embedders/embeddings-health.ts`) | Probes the hf-local socket | Unchanged, the guide says what it probes | REQ-011 |\n80: | `OllamaAdapter` and `OLLAMA_QUERY_TIMEOUT_MS` (`system-spec-kit/shared`) | Shared deadline for every query embedding | Unchanged. The deadline lives in the advisor's wrapper so other consumers keep 5,000 ms | `git diff --stat` shows no file under `system-spec-kit/shared` |\n81: | `/doctor:setup` | Five read-only legs | Update: sixth leg | `DOC/scripts/tests/run-all.sh` |\n82: | `/doctor:install` | Five printed steps | Update: the embedder route becomes step 5 and `/doctor:setup` step 6 | `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` |\n83: | `/doctor:skill-advisor` | Six routes | Update: seventh route | `skill-advisor-route-contract.test.cjs`, `route-validate.sh`, `doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` |\n84: | Command bridge inventory | 45 TypeScript rows with `embeddingText` | Update: the route's bridge becomes active like its six siblings | Both captures and the policy rollup |\n85: | Hook brief (`ADV/lib/render.ts`) | Renders the brief | Unchanged, by the operator's answer of 2026-11-12 | Golden briefs unchanged in `npm test` |\n86: \n87: Matrix axes for the degrade test: server reachable or absent, model pulled or missing, answer inside or past the deadline, model warm or cold. The test holds one row per failure value plus a warm row and a cold-inside-deadline row, six rows in total.\n88: <!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n89: \n90: ---\n91: \n92: <!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n93: ## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n94: \n95: Setup records the before numbers, the hook timing and the cold-load behaviour after an aborted call. Implementation adds the script, the deadline, the status fields, the warning, the route, the setup leg and the guide text in the waves `tasks.md` lists. Verification reruns the script, both captures, the floor, the rollup, the hook timing and both test suites. The ordered work and each task's check are in `tasks.md`.\n96: <!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n97: \n98: ---\n99: \n100: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n101: ## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n102: \n103: | Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n104: |-----------|-------|-------|\n105: | Unit | The prompt embedding with an injected adapter: warm, cold inside the deadline, absent, model missing, past the deadline and the warning | Vitest, `tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` with `VITEST` stubbed off inside the test |\n106: | Unit | Status `backend` states and `commandVectorCoverage` against fixture databases | Vitest, `tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` |\n107: | Integration | The route's plan-first contract, the setup leg and the install step | `bash DOC/scripts/tests/run-all.sh`, `bash DOC/scripts/route-validate.sh`, `node DOC/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` |\n108: | Integration | Captures, floor and rollup unchanged with the new bridge active | `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` with and without `--real-embedding`, `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs` |\n109: | Manual | The script on the build machine, once warm and once after the 5 minute unload | `node ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs` |\n110: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n111: \n112: ---\n113: \n114: <!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n115: ## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n116: \n117: | Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n118: |------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n119: | Ollama 0.40.15 with `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` | External | Green: running on 2026-11-12 | No measured numbers. The tests still run with an injected adapter |\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 120]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/plan.md\",\"offset\":60,\"limit\":60}"},"time":{"start":1794535037016,"end":1794535037141}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794535037145,"sessionID":"ses_e2d61a837fferT6vx7XBcnnvGb","part":{"partID":"prt_1d29f985900160fZvKgC5wrr7r","sessionID":"ses_e2d61a837fferT6vx7XBcnnvGb","messageID":"msg_1d29f8ee8001t8PEcoRFOWMvAh","type":"tool","id":"call_7550ee45ce7248aa843125c1","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/semantic-shadow-cosine.vitest.ts"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/semantic-shadow-cosine.vitest.ts, lines 1-215\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: Semantic Shadow Cosine Lane Tests\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: \n5: import { mkdtempSync, rmSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n6: import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\n7: import { join } from 'node:path';\n8: import { afterEach, beforeEach, describe, expect, it, vi } from 'vitest';\n9: \n10: const { embedDocument, embedQuery, createEmbeddingsProvider } = vi.hoisted(() => {\n11:   const embedDocument = vi.fn(async (text: string) => (\n12:     text.includes('changed')\n13:       ? new Float32Array([0, 1])\n14:       : new Float32Array([1, 0])\n15:   ));\n16:   const embedQuery = vi.fn(async () => new Float32Array([1, 0]));\n17:   return {\n18:     embedDocument,\n19:     embedQuery,\n20:     createEmbeddingsProvider: vi.fn(async () => ({\n21:       embedDocument,\n22:       embedQuery,\n23:       getProfile: () => ({\n24:         provider: 'mock',\n25:         model: 'fixture',\n26:         dim: 2,\n27:         slug: 'mock-fixture-2',\n28:       }),\n29:     })),\n30:   };\n31: });\n32: \n33: vi.mock('@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/factory.js', async (importOriginal) => {\n34:   const actual = await importOriginal<typeof import('@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/factory.js')>();\n35:   return {\n36:     ...actual,\n37:     createEmbeddingsProvider,\n38:   };\n39: });\n40: \n41: import {\n42:   closeDb,\n43:   getDb,\n44:   indexSkillMetadata,\n45:   initDb,\n46:   refreshSkillEmbeddings,\n47: } from '../../lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.js';\n48: import {\n49:   _semanticShadowTest,\n50:   clearSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding,\n51:   scoreSemanticShadowLane,\n52:   setSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding,\n53: } from '../../lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.js';\n54: import { scoreAdvisorPrompt } from '../../lib/scorer/fusion.js';\n55: import { createFixtureProjection } from '../../lib/scorer/projection.js';\n56: import type { AdvisorProjection, SkillProjection } from '../../lib/scorer/types.js';\n57: import { writeGraphMetadata } from '../fixtures/skill-graph-db.js';\n58: \n59: function buffer(values: readonly number[]): Buffer {\n60:   const vector = Float32Array.from(values);\n61:   return Buffer.from(vector.buffer, vector.byteOffset, vector.byteLength);\n62: }\n63: \n64: function skill(overrides: Partial<SkillProjection> & Pick<SkillProjection, 'id'>): SkillProjection {\n65:   return {\n66:     kind: 'skill',\n67:     family: 'system',\n68:     category: 'test',\n69:     name: overrides.id,\n70:     description: '',\n71:     keywords: [],\n72:     domains: [],\n73:     intentSignals: [],\n74:     derivedTriggers: [],\n75:     derivedKeywords: [],\n76:     sourcePath: null,\n77:     lifecycleStatus: 'active',\n78:     ...overrides,\n79:     id: overrides.id,\n80:   };\n81: }\n82: \n83: function writeSkill(skillRoot: string, skillId: string, description: string): void {\n84:   writeGraphMetadata(skillRoot, skillId);\n85:   writeFileSync(join(skillRoot, skillId, 'SKILL.md'), [\n86:     '---',\n87:     `name: ${skillId}`,\n88:     `description: \"${description}\"`,\n89:     '---',\n90:     '',\n91:   ].join('\\n'), 'utf8');\n92: }\n93: \n94: describe('semantic shadow cosine lane', () => {\n95:   let root: string;\n96:   let dbDir: string;\n97:   let skillRoot: string;\n98: \n99:   beforeEach(() => {\n100:     root = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'semantic-shadow-cosine-'));\n101:     dbDir = join(root, 'db');\n102:     skillRoot = join(root, 'skills');\n103:     initDb(dbDir);\n104:     embedDocument.mockClear();\n105:     embedQuery.mockClear();\n106:     createEmbeddingsProvider.mockClear();\n107:   });\n108: \n109:   afterEach(() => {\n110:     clearSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding();\n111:     closeDb();\n112:     rmSync(root, { recursive: true, force: true });\n113:     vi.restoreAllMocks();\n114:   });\n115: \n116:   it('applies the embedding schema migration idempotently', () => {\n117:     closeDb();\n118:     initDb(dbDir);\n119:     closeDb();\n120:     initDb(dbDir);\n121: \n122:     const columns = getDb().prepare('PRAGMA table_info(skill_nodes)').all() as Array<{ name: string }>;\n123:     expect(columns.map((column) => column.name)).toEqual(expect.arrayContaining([\n124:       'embedding',\n125:       'embedding_model_id',\n126:       'embedding_content_hash',\n127:     ]));\n128:   });\n129: \n130:   it('embeds changed skill descriptions and skips matching hash/model rows', async () => {\n131:     writeSkill(skillRoot, 'alpha', 'stable local embedding workflow');\n132:     indexSkillMetadata(skillRoot);\n133: \n134:     const first = await refreshSkillEmbeddings(skillRoot);\n135:     const second = await refreshSkillEmbeddings(skillRoot);\n136: \n137:     expect(first).toEqual(expect.objectContaining({ embedded: 1, skipped: 0, failed: 0 }));\n138:     expect(second).toEqual(expect.objectContaining({ embedded: 0, skipped: 1, failed: 0 }));\n139:     expect(embedDocument).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);\n140: \n141:     writeSkill(skillRoot, 'alpha', 'changed local embedding workflow');\n142:     indexSkillMetadata(skillRoot);\n143:     const third = await refreshSkillEmbeddings(skillRoot);\n144: \n145:     expect(third).toEqual(expect.objectContaining({ embedded: 1, failed: 0 }));\n146:     expect(embedDocument).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(2);\n147:   });\n148: \n149:   it('computes cosine lane matches from cached skill vectors', () => {\n150:     writeSkill(skillRoot, 'alpha', 'north vector');\n151:     writeSkill(skillRoot, 'beta', 'east vector');\n152:     indexSkillMetadata(skillRoot);\n153:     getDb().prepare(`\n154:       UPDATE skill_nodes\n155:       SET embedding = ?, embedding_model_id = ?, embedding_content_hash = ?\n156:       WHERE id = ?\n157:     `).run(buffer([1, 0]), 'mock-fixture-2', 'hash-alpha', 'alpha');\n158:     getDb().prepare(`\n159:       UPDATE skill_nodes\n160:       SET embedding = ?, embedding_model_id = ?, embedding_content_hash = ?\n161:       WHERE id = ?\n162:     `).run(buffer([0, 1]), 'mock-fixture-2', 'hash-beta', 'beta');\n163: \n164:     const projection: AdvisorProjection = {\n165:       skills: [skill({ id: 'alpha' }), skill({ id: 'beta' })],\n166:       edges: [],\n167:       generatedAt: '2026-05-13T00:00:00.000Z',\n168:       source: 'sqlite',\n169:     };\n170:     setSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding('north', new Float32Array([1, 0]));\n171: \n172:     expect(_semanticShadowTest.cosineSimilarity(new Float32Array([1, 0]), new Float32Array([1, 0]))).toBe(1);\n173:     expect(_semanticShadowTest.cosineSimilarity(new Float32Array([1, 0]), new Float32Array([0, 1]))).toBe(0);\n174:     expect(scoreSemanticShadowLane('north', projection)).toEqual([\n175:       {\n176:         skillId: 'alpha',\n177:         lane: 'semantic_shadow',\n178:         score: 1,\n179:         evidence: ['cosine:1.0000'],\n180:         shadowOnly: false,\n181:       },\n182:     ]);\n183:   });\n184: \n185:   it('keeps semantic matches from overturning an explicit top route', () => {\n186:     const projection = createFixtureProjection([\n187:       skill({\n188:         id: 'alpha',\n189:         description: 'plain implementation route',\n190:         intentSignals: ['alpha exact route'],\n191:       }),\n192:       skill({\n193:         id: 'beta',\n194:         description: 'semantic shadow should not promote beta',\n195:       }),\n196:     ]);\n197: \n198:     const withShadow = scoreAdvisorPrompt('alpha exact route', {\n199:       workspaceRoot: process.cwd(),\n200:       projection,\n201:     });\n202:     const withoutShadow = scoreAdvisorPrompt('alpha exact route', {\n203:       workspaceRoot: process.cwd(),\n204:       projection,\n205:       disabledLanes: ['semantic_shadow'],\n206:     });\n207: \n208:     const semantic = withShadow.recommendations[0]?.laneContributions.find((lane) => lane.lane === 'semantic_shadow');\n209: \n210:     expect(withShadow.topSkill).toBe(withoutShadow.topSkill);\n211:     expect(withShadow.topSkill).toBe('alpha');\n212:     expect(semantic?.weightedScore).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n213:     expect(semantic?.shadowOnly).toBe(false);\n214:   });\n215: });","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/semantic-shadow-cosine.vitest.ts, lines 1-215\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: Semantic Shadow Cosine Lane Tests\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: \n5: import { mkdtempSync, rmSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n6: import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\n7: import { join } from 'node:path';\n8: import { afterEach, beforeEach, describe, expect, it, vi } from 'vitest';\n9: \n10: const { embedDocument, embedQuery, createEmbeddingsProvider } = vi.hoisted(() => {\n11:   const embedDocument = vi.fn(async (text: string) => (\n12:     text.includes('changed')\n13:       ? new Float32Array([0, 1])\n14:       : new Float32Array([1, 0])\n15:   ));\n16:   const embedQuery = vi.fn(async () => new Float32Array([1, 0]));\n17:   return {\n18:     embedDocument,\n19:     embedQuery,\n20:     createEmbeddingsProv